attempts.prompt:
Korean webtoon panel, digitally inked and coloured by a professional webtoon studio. Crisp black ink with tapered strokes, heavier on the outer silhouette, the jaw, the hair mass and where forms overlap. Flat local colour with one hard-edged cool cel shadow per material. One named key light: its colour washes smoothly over the lit side. If the scene names a back light, it draws a thin crisp rim along the figure's silhouette. Everything else stays flat. Muted cool base palette of slate, navy and grey-blue, so the light source and the character's signature colour carry the saturation. Background simplified and lower in contrast than the characters. Small crisp highlights; glossy specular only on metal and wet surfaces.

Hand-made webtoon colouring: each garment has only a few large, opaque, clean-edged shadow shapes, placed in its real folds; no scattered translucent streaks, zigzag shards or crumpled-foil folds. Worn cloth shows a few small frayed notches and loose threads, never sawtooth edges along every edge. Plain shoes and clothes with no logos, stripes or brand marks. Every strap, buckle, pocket and seam is attached and has a purpose; no stray stitch marks. Matte skin, hair and stone; no 3D, low-poly or plastic look.

Use case: illustration-story. Asset: S24 CHIBI gag-pose model sheet, explicitly chibi under the project's A5b rules. One native 1536x1024 landscape PNG. Use Image 1, her final front master, for all colours, facial identity, grey perm, faded floral nape scarf, checked apron, purple tracksuit, pink rubber slippers, upper-left gold tooth, LEFT prosthetic and RIGHT steel ladle.
Exactly EIGHT complete full-body figures in a FOUR-column by TWO-row arrangement with generous clear gaps, no borders, no labels or text. Every figure is exactly about TWO-AND-A-HALF HEADS tall, an enlarged round head over a short but broad strong body; unmistakably a weathered bossy 62-year-old auntie with wrinkles, sharp brows and a wrestler's shoulders, never a baby, never a pretty young woman. Same design simplified into clean flat cel shapes, same head size in all cells. Solid flat #E9E9EC throughout, neutral upper-left key, only tiny contact shadows. No scene, props on ground or scale silhouette.
Pose order TOP ROW left to right:
(1) planted broad stance, huge gold-toothed grin, metal LEFT hand on hip, natural RIGHT hand holding her long steel ladle upright beside her;
(2) scolding furiously, mouth wide, ladle raised high in her flesh RIGHT hand, metal LEFT fist at hip, a tiny anger vein mark;
(3) deadpan with arms folded across chest, her RIGHT fingers still visibly gripping the ladle that lies diagonally across the folded arms, left metal forearm correctly attached beneath, narrow line eyes;
(4) reading someone's body OFF-PANEL, bending forward with head strongly cocked and suspicious narrowed eyes, RIGHT-hand ladle pointing slightly downward toward the off-panel patient, LEFT mechanical palm resting on her own hip.
BOTTOM ROW:
(5) a huge belly laugh, body leaning back, eyes squeezed shut and mouth wide showing upper LEFT gold tooth, metal LEFT palm on her belly, RIGHT hand still holding ladle down to the side;
(6) firm block stance with feet wide, metal LEFT open palm thrust outward in a 'stop' gesture (three fingers plus thumb), flesh RIGHT hand holds the ladle vertically beside her, one stern raised brow;
(7) comic surprise as her metal LEFT arm twitches on its own, eyes wide as dots, one sweat drop, shoulder flinching toward that arm, RIGHT hand keeps the ladle safely gripped;
(8) marching forward in pink slippers, one sole lifted slightly in a clear step, stern determined grin, RIGHT hand points the ladle forward at shoulder height, metal LEFT arm bends back with her stride, two short graphic motion ticks by the slipper.
All poses remain front or front three-quarter so the side locks are easy to read. Never mirror the costume or arms: her anatomical LEFT arm is gunmetal from just above elbow, blue painted wave on outer forearm, EXACTLY THREE thick fingers plus ONE opposed thumb. Her anatomical RIGHT arm is flesh, the ladle is always in that natural right hand. Simplify metal digits into four unmistakable chunky shapes; NO fourth long finger or rear pinkie. Preserve the single large round ladle bowl, straight handle, correct grip and two arms per figure. Natural right hand has five digits, simplified but correctly grasping the prop. No extra tools, food, scenery, new props, lettering, speech bubbles or numbers.
Auntie Geum Okran: a short, broad 62-year-old Korean woman, 155 cm, with a wrestler's shoulders and forearms; a sun-browned, deeply lined face, sharp black eyes, one gold tooth; short permed grey hair under a faded floral headscarf; a red-and-white checked apron over a faded purple tracksuit with the sleeves pushed up; pink rubber slippers; her left arm from just above the elbow is a battered gunmetal prosthetic of plates and rivets with a faded painted blue wave on the forearm, three thick fingers and a thumb; a big long-handled steel ladle in her right hand.
Explicit exceptions for this designated chibi sheet: 2.5-head short bodies, round heads and gag dot/line eyes ARE REQUIRED, unlike the full-size sheets. Preserve her age and blunt strong persona. The generic negative block's five-finger rule applies ONLY to her natural right hand. Metal LEFT hand has FOUR total digits, THREE fingers and ONE thumb.

No text, letters, numbers, speech bubbles, captions, sound-effect lettering, interface windows or readable signs. Emblems without letters are fine; no brand logos or wordmarks. Not a 3D render, not a photograph, no photographic background. No airbrushed skin, no plastic gloss on skin or hair, no haze or bloom over the whole image, no depth-of-field blur, no lens flare unless a real camera flash is in the scene. No watermark or signature. Correct hands with five fingers. No chibi proportions unless the brief says chibi. No compressed or stubby bodies, no shortened legs or torsos, no oversized heads; no people out of scale with the doors, vehicles and buildings around them; no figures floating off the floor or breaking the scene's perspective.

FINAL LOCK: this is the brief's intentional CHIBI sheet, 2.5 heads, eight poses. Every metal LEFT hand has exactly THREE fingers plus ONE thumb, four total. Only natural RIGHT hands have five digits and hold the ladle.
